{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch-sonnet5/runs/eval-INC-219-r1-holdout/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "## Summary\n\nINC-219 (arrival times shown in UTC instead of destination port local time) is fixed.\n\n**Root cause:** `src/eta/local.ts:22` hardcoded `\"UTC\"` as the timezone when formatting arrival timestamps, ignoring the port's actual `timezone` field from the registry.\n\n**Fix:** Changed `stamp(eta, \"UTC\")` → `stamp(eta, port.timezone)`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Both acceptance-criteria cases pass: `SGSIN` → `2026-03-01 20:00`, `NLRTM` → `2026-03-01 13:00`\n- Unknown ports still correctly throw `RangeError`\n- Added a regression test in `test/eta.test.ts` covering non-UTC timezones (the existing test only used Felixstowe, which is UTC+0 in winter and happened to mask this bug)\n- Full `npm run check` passes: 27/27 tests, codegen verify clean\n\nChanges are in `src/eta/local.ts` and `test/eta.test.ts`, not yet committed — let me know if you'd like me to commit.", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9iv8PmuvWQkQ3d83ie", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "98316c57-d9fc-4b6b-b3cc-eb670d25767f", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:46:30.742Z", "type": "assistant"}
